Runtime mechanism lineage acknowledgment
----------------------------------------

According to the lineage declared by the mechanism's author, Dani designed
the runtime rank-1 integration with a switchable lambda dial, originating in
qwen38 and ported by him to DeepSeek V4.0-Flash (0731), before the 2026-10-15
handover. This project's 1017 integration is a third generation in that
declared lineage, using different pqhaz directions without recalibrating them.
This is an attribution of the author's account, not independent verification
of his Git history or service, nor a claim of original authorship of the
underlying mathematical projection. See README.md and ATTRIBUTION.md for the
reported milestones and the separate component and data credits.

According to the lineage declared by its authors, the reference implementation
ported here and the CUDA Graph fix documented as rank1g are by Pocharlies
(@oppocharliesllmbot / pocharlies-org); mechanism design remains credited to Dani.
The private reference is pocharlies-org/qwen38-recipe-handover,
deepseek-rank1-refusal/, declared commit
0af2f04da7545f1687fe7aae85250ca89929304b. It includes the 0001-rank1-projection
and 0002-per-request-lambda patches, extraction script and FASE1-3 documents.
Its adapted patterns include the device lambda tensor mutated in place (never
rebound), target/drafter role separation, lambda in prefix-cache hash identity,
and cache_salt per request. Prior implementations attributed to Pocharlies are
the resident qwen38 refusal dial and images/deepseek-v4-rank1 for 0731. No public
URL for those implementations has been verified. These are attributed lineage
statements, not an independent Git-history or live-service audit. The current
1017 implementation remains a third generation with pqhaz directions not
recalibrated by this project. See ATTRIBUTION.md for identifiers and boundaries.

